{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"mcporter call exa.web_search_exa query='site:forum.intervals.icu \\\"October 2026\\\" \\\"workout\\\" \\\"export\\\" \\\"HR\\\"' numResults=5\"","aggregated_output":"Title: Latest\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/latest?no_definitions=true&page=2\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\n## Activity HRV (not Wellness)\n\nAuthor: @miguelpais\nReplies: 41\nLast updated: 15 October 2026 20:27 UTC\n\nHello everyone, I’ve just selected the option on my Garmin edge 530 to log HRV and I’ve seen that this outputs some values onto the FIT file. I understand Garmin uses this to present their “Performance Baseline” metric…\n\n...\n\n## All fields from Garmin activity\n\nAuthor: @Povedano\nReplies: 164\nLast updated: 15 October 2026 09:14 UTC\n\nI have been creating some activity custom fields using the powerful “Fit file field” option on intervals.icu custom fields. I’ve been able to extract all this information from my Garmin sessions (F7 + HRM-Pro): They …\n\n...\n\nHi @david – two API wishes from the garmin-intervals-bridge (self-hosted, open source: since Garmin filters the files it hands to partners, it fetches the original FIT from Garmin Connect). 1.\n\n...\n\n## Mi-scale-exporter - Android app with direct intervals.icu upload (Xiaomi Smart Scales)\n\nAuthor: @daktak\nReplies: 0\nLast updated: 15 October 2026 08:16 UTC\n\nUpdated to support direct upload to intervals.icu for weight and body fat %.\n\n...\n\n## Merging FIT/GPX/etc. files\n\nAuthor: @Wayde_Bendus\nReplies: 13\nLast updated: 15 October 2026 06:03 UTC\n\nMy typical setup is to run a workout in Zwift and simultaneously record the HR, Power, Cadence, and Moxy data (SMO2 & THb) on my Garmin. However, the other night my Garmin didn’t pick of the power data from my trainer, …\n\n...\n\n## Coros support added\n\nAuthor: @david\nReplies: 106\nLast updated: 15 October 2026 03:16 UTC\n\nIntervals.icu can now download completed activities, wellness data (sleep, resting HR) and upload planned workouts to Coros. Look for the Coros box in /settings: If you enable uploading of planned workouts the next w…\n\n...\n\n## Heart Rate Graph: free Android live HR display for Bluetooth sensors\n\nAuthor: @Jorge_Va_Dev\nReplies: 0\nLast updated: 15 October 2026 02:56 UTC\n\nHi, I’m the independent developer of Heart Rate Graph, a free Android app for viewing your heart rate while you train with an external Bluetooth sensor. It displays a live BPM graph, coloured training zones and time spe…\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals Companion v4 updates\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-companion-v4-updates/133092\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\n# Intervals Companion v4 updates\n\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-companion-v4-updates/133092\nCategory: External Projects\nCreated: 17 October 2026 15:14 UTC\nPosts on this page: 19\nPage: 1\n\nAuthor: @spmcewen\nPost date: 17 October 2026 15:14 UTC\n\nFirst, thanks to everyone who has supported the app. That support is what made this update possible.\n\nA few important points up front:\n\n- IC+ is a new tier for supporters. Yes, another plus-sign subscription. Everyone loves these, right?.. right? Don’t worry, though. Everything in v3 works the way it did previously. Supporting the app unlocks IC+, with a set of extra features that build on everything in v3.\n- AI features are optional. They don’t change anything from v3 and can be disabled completely in the setting (or long press a card to dismiss). IC+ still unlocks a few other goodies.\n- All AI features use Apple’s Private Cloud Compute. Apple built this for security and privacy, so your data is protected end to end and isn’t kept or visible to anyone, including Apple. AI text generation and the chat need iOS 27 with Apple Intelligence. Analysis tiles appear on any supported device. The written analysis requires Apple Intelligence. Personally, I have found the AI analysis to be useful at identifying trends across data and date ranges. This round of Apple’s AI is also much more capable than the previous on device models. The prompts and functionality will likely get updates as more users come on board and report back about how well (or not!) this works. As always, keep in mind that AI can be wrong and you should always use your own judgment.\n\nIC+ Features\n\n- AI analysis of activities, readiness and sleep scores, your fitness trend, and daily wellness, plus an Ask AI chat that can answer questions about your data and build workouts from text prompts.\n- Suggested Workouts, Today & Week Ahead Analysis: a daily summary of your week so far, plus a suggested next workout.\n- Workout Builder Create a workout from a text prompt and add to your calendar.\n- Simple Training Goals: tell the app whether you’re building, maintaining, targeting a date, or following a training plan, and it helps inform the other AI features.\n- Sync intervals.icu daily wellness to Apple Health: weight, HRV, resting HR and more from intervals.icu can sync to Apple Health automatically.\n- Automatic edits and deletions to Apple Health Editing or deleting activities on intervals.icu will sync back to Apple Health automatically.\n- Strava export Push activities from intervals.icu to Strava, including mountain bike dynamics as the Strava activity description. Rather than having Strava access to your Apple Health data, or relying on other apps to push to Strava.\n\n...\n\n- Support for Apple’s recovery HRV (rMSSD) in readiness score and HRV charts\n- Full-screen activity map can show the multi-graph, and the map follows the location as you drag a graph marker\n- Garmin mountain bike dynamics (grit, flow, jumps) in activity details and on route map\n- Ride Cave added as a platform to sync activities to Apple Health\n- Calendar subscription link in calendar settings\n- Apple Watch sync can be filtered by activity type\n- Apple Shortcut to trigger automatic workout sync to Apple Watch\n- Favorite wellness metrics to pin them to the top of the metrics edit sheet, plus many more custom wellness metrics supported\n- Layout, tab bar, and toolbar improvements with support for iPhone Duo.\n- Many other small UI tweaks and improvements\n\n...\n\nAuthor: @spmcewen\nPost date: 20 October 2026 17:29 UTC\n\nSince Strava is taking a while to approve my API increase request, and my readiness currently looks like this…\n\n..I’m just going to keep going. Here are some new user requested features that will be in 4.0:\n\n- Bulk export prior Apple workouts as FIT files for manually importing to intervals.icu. Find this on the Sync screen, Apple → Intervals.icu settings\n- Update HRV rMSSD and Baevsky SI using an Apple Watch Mindfulness breathe session. Enable toolbar icon in Metrics screen settings. Option to automatically sync when new breath sessions are recorded.\n- Custom metrics sync field for awake time during sleep\n\n...\n\nPost date: 21 October 2026 16:38 UTC\n\n4.0 is submitted to Apple for approval. I’m moving forward without the Strava API increase request being resolved. Reading their developer forums, it sounds like these can take many weeks and even months to be processed. Users will see a user limit error when connecting to Strava until it gets increased.\n\nDue to the scale of the changes in 4.0, I’m using Apple’s 7-day slow rollout option, so 4.0 will show up as an automatic update over the next week or so, after I get through the approval process (fingers crossed!)\n\n...\n\nI was notified that 4.0 is approved. That’s the fastest approval I have ever seen Apple do. I wonder if they ramped up for the Duo launch, and all the apps trying to get through the approval pipeline before it is available. It should be showing in the App Store now.\n\n...\n\nOne feature that would be really useful is settings sync between devices. I use Companion on both iPhone and iPad, and right now every change has to be duplicated manually.\n\niCloud sync would be ideal, but even a simple Export / Import Settings option would already be very useful — both for keeping devices aligned and as a backup.\n\n---\n\nTitle: MyTrainPal - AI Assistant connected to Intervals - Page 15 - AI Tools - Intervals.icu Forum\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/mytrainpal-ai-assistant-connected-to-intervals/122009?page=15\nPublished: 2026-02-10T13:20:38.000Z\nAuthor: Krzysztof\nHighlights:\nI’ve tweaked the route generation parameters to introduce more hills and turns along the way.\n\n...\n\nERG is currently disabled at the start because I found that it can behave unpredictably if it is enabled before the trainer begins reporting power. If I find a reliable way to handle that, I’ll make ERG remember and preserve the previously selected setting.\n\n...\n\nDario_Cardona_Fernan 12 September 2026 12:13 286 \n\nAl subir entrenamientos a INTERVALS sigue haciendolo mal. Esta es una sesion que ha subido de 4x800mtr de carrera a pie: 20m ramp Z1-Z2 HR Calentamiento 20m Z1-Z2\n\n- 3m Z4 HR 800m Z4 (149-165 bpm)\n- Rest 1m30 Z1 HR Recuperacion 90s Z1\n- 3m Z4 HR 800m Z4 (149-165 bpm)\n- Rest 1m30 Z1 HR Recuperacion 90s Z1\n- 3m Z4 HR 800m Z4 (149-165 bpm)\n- Rest 1m30 Z1 HR Recuperacion 90s Z1\n- 3m Z4 HR 800m Z4 (149-165 bpm)\n- Rest 1m30 Z1 HR Recuperacion 90s Z1\n- 10m Z1 HR Enfriamiento 10m Z1\n- 20m ramp Z1-Z2 (110-135 bpm)\n- Press lap 4x\n- 800m Z4 (149-165 bpm)\n- 90s Z1 HR\n- Press lap\n- 10m Z1 (<115 bpm)\n\n Krzysztof 12 September 2026 15:41 287 \n\nHi @Dario_Cardona_Fernan ,\n\nThanks for providing these details. This clear bug in export to Intervals is high on my list. Expect it to be fixed soon.\n\n...\n\nBug with the charts after workout. The ramp thing is fixed but my workout yesterday was 3 x 11 sweet spot. Looked fine in calendar before workout. 3 green block. Workout was completed fine in erg and you can’t see the power line when viewed but the graph is totally random.\n\n...\n\nHope you had a nice time.\n\nthe charts are definitely wonky compared to the actual efforts now.\n\n...\n\nKrzysztof 22 September 2026 17:21 299 \n\nHi,\n\nall systems are operational. Probably some intermittent hiccup.\n\nBtw. the charts should not be wonky anymore and follow the actual efforts. This will apply to the new workouts as the charts are generated during import though. Let me know please if you notice any more issues.\n\n Krzysztof 25 September 2026 14:05 300 \n\nA small update for the strength workouts. If you have Strava connected, every strength workout will be exported with corrected mapping to Strava exercises, so you can track it there as well if you want.\n\n Jamie_Bishop 28 September 2026 08:29 301 \n\nCharts are improving for workouts, but not great for an IRL race, makes it look like a TT effort which couldn’y be further from the truth. \n\n Krzysztof 1 October 2026 07:39 302 \n\nThanks @Jamie_Bishop , one step closer to getting them perfect More updates to come soon.\n\n---\n\nTitle: Uncategorized\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/c/uncategorized/1\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\n## Strength training exercises as intervals/laps on the timeline — HR per exercise possible?\n\nAuthor: @Meejtie\nReplies: 15\nLast updated: 24 October 2026 10:25 UTC\n\nHi all, I’ve been trying to get more out of my strength training data in Intervals.icu and hoping someone has solved this already. Here’s my setup: I create structured strength workouts in Garmin Connect (exercises, …\n\n...\n\nVersion 0.9.75 of alphaHRV is available for update. This release finally provides every user the option to display real time evolution of (RespRate/alpha-1) vs Heart Rate Below an example of the data field when this ne…\n\n...\n\n## Intervals in old activities auto-updated. Tried to re-analyse and cannot get back to laps\n\nAuthor: @PietroSun\nReplies: 1\nLast updated: 22 October 2026 09:40 UTC\n\nBefore, from an older screenshot I had posted on Strava Checked this activity today, and the intervals were different. I assume because I had reprocessed activities after updating my HR / pace stats. That’s okay - th…\n\n...\n\n## API requests from GitHub Actions return HTTP 403\n\nAuthor: @NiinaKos\nReplies: 1\nLast updated: 21 October 2026 12:30 UTC\n\nSubject: API requests from GitHub Actions return HTTP 403 Hi, I’m trying to automate the daily export of my training and wellness data using the Intervals.icu API and a private GitHub Actions workflow. API requests us…\n\n---\n\nTitle: Latest\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/latest?page=5\nPublished: N/A\nAuthor: N/A\nHighlights:\n## Cannot combine HR and pace-based intervals in single workout?\n\nAuthor: @gecks\nReplies: 13\nLast updated: 21 October 2026 06:22 UTC\n\nI have been able to use %HR just fine for interval-less runs: Easy - 43m 50-70% HR and these appear as green in the workout visualizer and work fine on garmin: However if I do the same for a warmup/cooldown before/…\n\n...\n\n## Hide Notes on exported Intervals.icu calendar?\n\nAuthor: @Mark_Snackey\nReplies: 9\nLast updated: 21 October 2026 06:12 UTC\n\nHi, I enjoy the feature to export the Intervals.icu calendar so I can see my planned workouts in my normal day-to-day Google Calendar. However, I’d like to hide the Notes, since they’re generally not relevant on that ca…\n\n...\n\nYa puedo ver la variabilidad de la frecuencia cardíaca en el calendario, pero cuando trato de exportar los datos de bienestar, la columna de la variabilidad viene vacía. Que puede ser\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
